.TH INTRO 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
intro \- commands available in FUZIX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
man intro
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use man followed by a command name to read its manual, for example man sh,
man cp, man less, man vi or man tcl. Games are in section 6: man wump and
man hamurabi. Space advances the pager, Enter shows a line, and q returns
to the shell. Ctrl-C interrupts the foreground program.
.PP
Use shutdown to save the filesystem and stop the machine. Files in your
session persist across launches. Run ls /bin to list installed commands; help summarizes shell features.
.PP
Shell scripts, pipelines, redirection, loops and command substitution are
available through sh. Editors are vi (Rift), levee, vile and ed. With ed, use q
to quit, or Q to discard changes.
.PP
Other useful commands include ls, cat, cp, mv, ln, rm, mkdir, rmdir, pwd,
touch, chmod, chown, chgrp, mkfifo, mknod, basename, dirname, find, dd, tar,
head, tail, wc, grep, fgrep, sed, sort, uniq, cut, tr, tee, comm, rev, expand,
colrm, od, sum, cmp, diff, join, split, fmt, column, pr, col, tsort, cksum,
more, less, clear, stty, tty, mktemp, ps, kill, sleep, env, printenv, id,
whoami, uname, date, which, xargs, time, nice, nohup, groups, logname, df,
du, sync, test, true, false, seq, yes, expr, awk, make, m4, dc, cowsay
and tcl. The bf interpreter runs Brainfuck source files.
.PP
Networking tools include ifconfig, ping, telnet, telnetd, host, nslookup,
dig, htget, echoping and ntpdate. Use man htget for HTTP downloads and
man dig for DNS queries.
